WEBVTT

00:00:02.803 --> 00:00:04.310
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.316 --> 00:00:05.885
Let's say good night to your brother.

00:00:06.088 --> 00:00:07.148
Night, Sam.

00:00:07.272 --> 00:00:08.652
Hey, Dean.

00:00:08.677 --> 00:00:10.206
Daddy! Hey, buddy.

00:00:11.127 --> 00:00:12.734
Sweet dreams, Sam.

00:00:16.892 --> 00:00:19.370
Dad's missing. I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.317
The trail for dad, it's getting colder.

00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:24.031
Every day. You don't think I want
to find dad as much as you do?

00:00:24.055 --> 00:00:25.433
I know you do. Find dad.

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:27.750
Mom's gone. She isn't coming back.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.151
Don't talk about her like that.

00:00:55.344 --> 00:00:56.599
Mommy?

00:00:58.259 --> 00:01:00.188
Hey, sweetie.

00:01:00.464 --> 00:01:04.413
Why aren't you in bed?
There's something in my closet.

00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:21.071
See?

00:01:21.106 --> 00:01:22.385
There's nothing there.

00:01:23.763 --> 00:01:26.702
You're sure? I'm sure.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.990
Now, come on.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.101
Into bed.

00:01:43.544 --> 00:01:45.167
I don't like this house.

00:01:45.782 --> 00:01:47.381
You're just not used to it yet.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:54.045
But you and your brother and me,
we are going to be very happy here.

00:01:54.596 --> 00:01:55.604
I promise.

00:01:58.209 --> 00:01:59.864
I love you.

00:02:07.664 --> 00:02:08.417
The chair.

00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:10.712
Okay.

00:02:11.351 --> 00:02:12.329
Right.

00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:17.258
The chair.

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:21.572
Just to be safe.

00:02:53.812 --> 00:02:57.348
Please, god, don't let it be rats.

00:03:17.057 --> 00:03:18.294
Terrific.

00:05:15.885 --> 00:05:16.578
All right.

00:05:16.603 --> 00:05:18.400
I've been cruising some websites.

00:05:18.505 --> 00:05:20.899
Think I found a few
candidates for our next gig.

00:05:22.206 --> 00:05:24.963
A fishing trawler found
off the coast of Cali.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.486
Its crew vanished.

00:05:26.717 --> 00:05:30.200
And we got some cattle
mutilations in west Texas.

00:05:30.682 --> 00:05:31.299
Hey!

00:05:33.131 --> 00:05:35.193
Am I boring you with
this hunting-Evil stuff?

00:05:35.733 --> 00:05:37.815
No, I'm listening. Keep going.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.596
And here a Sacramento man
shot himself in the head...

00:05:43.039 --> 00:05:44.273
Three times.

00:05:46.711 --> 00:05:48.754
Any of these things
blowing up your skirt, pal?

00:05:52.783 --> 00:05:54.817
Wait, I've seen this. Seen what?

00:06:01.678 --> 00:06:02.791
What are you doing?

00:06:11.132 --> 00:06:12.872
Dean, I know where we have to go next.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:13.584
Where?

00:06:14.213 --> 00:06:15.151
Back home.

00:06:15.965 --> 00:06:16.989
Back to Kansas.

00:06:18.383 --> 00:06:20.258
Okay, random. Where'd that come from?

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.152
All right, um...

00:06:22.192 --> 00:06:24.521
This photo was taken in
front of our old house, right?

00:06:24.606 --> 00:06:25.821
The house where mom died?

00:06:27.266 --> 00:06:27.922
Yeah.

00:06:27.999 --> 00:06:31.161
It didn't burn down right? I mean not
completely, they rebuilt it, right?

00:06:31.238 --> 00:06:33.590
I guess so, yeah. What the
hell are you talking about?

00:06:33.621 --> 00:06:35.831
Okay, look, this is gonna sound crazy,

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:37.944
But the people who
live in our old house,

00:06:39.212 --> 00:06:40.851
I think they might be in danger.

00:06:41.196 --> 00:06:43.566
Why would you think that? Uh...

00:06:43.624 --> 00:06:45.646
Just, um... look, just...

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.030
You got to trust me on this, okay?

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.736
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa. Trust you? Yeah.

00:06:51.254 --> 00:06:53.158
You got to give me a
little bit more than that.

00:06:53.204 --> 00:06:54.936
I can't really explain, it is all.

00:06:55.141 --> 00:06:57.665
Well, tough. I'm not going
anywhere until you do.

00:07:02.327 --> 00:07:04.023
I have these nightmares.

00:07:04.324 --> 00:07:05.728
I've noticed.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:10.514
And sometimes they come true.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:14.574
Come again?

00:07:15.437 --> 00:07:16.116
Look, Dean...

00:07:17.309 --> 00:07:18.773
I dreamt about Jessica's death

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.484
For days before it happened.

00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:26.827
Sane people have weird dreams, man.
I'm sure it's just a coincidence.

00:07:27.376 --> 00:07:30.510
No, I dreamt about the blood dripping,
her on the ceiling, the fire, everything,

00:07:30.522 --> 00:07:32.389
And I didn't do anything
'cause I didn't believe it.

00:07:32.447 --> 00:07:34.067
Now I'm dreaming about that tree,

00:07:34.236 --> 00:07:37.087
About our house, and some woman
inside screaming for help. I mean,

00:07:37.276 --> 00:07:39.716
That's where it all started, man.
This has to mean something, right?

00:07:41.991 --> 00:07:42.824
I don't know.

00:07:43.844 --> 00:07:46.025
What do you mean you
don't know, Dean? This...

00:07:46.143 --> 00:07:47.832
This woman might be in danger.

00:07:47.891 --> 00:07:52.031
This might be the thing that killed mom and
Jessica. All right, just slow down,would you?

00:07:56.066 --> 00:07:58.670
I mean, first you're telling
me that you've got this Shining

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.756
and then you tell me that
I've got to go back home,

00:08:02.999 --> 00:08:03.922
Especially when...

00:08:05.905 --> 00:08:07.009
When what?

00:08:08.427 --> 00:08:10.714
When I swore to myself that
I would never go back there.

00:08:22.115 --> 00:08:24.062
Dean, we have to check this out.

00:08:25.208 --> 00:08:26.608
Just to make sure.

00:08:33.936 --> 00:08:35.027
I know we do.

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:55.066
You gonna be all right, man?

00:08:56.967 --> 00:08:58.793
Let me get back to you on that.

00:09:06.865 --> 00:09:07.358
Yes?

00:09:07.628 --> 00:09:08.988
Sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:09:09.099 --> 00:09:11.492
But we're with the
federal... I'm Sam Winchester

00:09:11.726 --> 00:09:13.486
And this is my brother, Dean.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.884
Um...we used to live here.

00:09:16.799 --> 00:09:19.169
You know, we were just driving by, and

00:09:19.222 --> 00:09:21.603
We were wondering if we
could come see the old place.

00:09:21.664 --> 00:09:22.825
Winchester...

00:09:24.362 --> 00:09:25.817
That is so funny.

00:09:26.013 --> 00:09:29.333
You know, I, I think I found some
of your photos the other night.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.025
You did?

00:09:34.291 --> 00:09:36.441
Okay. Come on in.

00:09:48.381 --> 00:09:50.446
Juice, juice, juice!

00:09:50.481 --> 00:09:52.399
Juice, juice,  juice!

00:09:52.422 --> 00:09:56.293
That's Richie. He's
kind of a juice junkie.

00:09:56.532 --> 00:09:59.499
But, hey, at least he won't get scurvy.

00:10:00.755 --> 00:10:01.857
Sari,

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:04.368
This is Sam and Dean.

00:10:04.416 --> 00:10:06.351
They used to live here. Hi.

00:10:06.879 --> 00:10:07.817
Hey, Sari.

00:10:08.768 --> 00:10:10.070
So, you just moved in?

00:10:10.128 --> 00:10:11.853
Uh, yeah, from Wichita.

00:10:11.955 --> 00:10:13.375
You got family here?

00:10:14.466 --> 00:10:16.436
No, I just, uh...

00:10:17.598 --> 00:10:20.759
Um, needed a fresh start. That's all.

00:10:21.888 --> 00:10:24.089
So new town,

00:10:24.199 --> 00:10:25.317
New job

00:10:25.501 --> 00:10:27.333
I mean, as soon as I find one,

00:10:27.737 --> 00:10:29.001
New house.

00:10:31.056 --> 00:10:32.816
So, how you liking it so far?

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.783
Well, uh, all due respect
to your childhood home,

00:10:37.875 --> 00:10:41.320
I mean, I'm sure you have
lots of happy memories here,

00:10:41.778 --> 00:10:44.051
But this place has its issues.

00:10:44.326 --> 00:10:45.536
What do you mean?

00:10:46.909 --> 00:10:48.706
Well, it's just getting old

00:10:49.109 --> 00:10:51.235
Like, the wiring, you know? We've got

00:10:51.363 --> 00:10:53.471
Flickering lights almost hourly.

00:10:53.581 --> 00:10:54.827
Oh, that's too bad.

00:10:55.304 --> 00:10:56.330
What else?

00:10:56.678 --> 00:11:00.986
Um...sink's backed up.
There's rats in the basement.

00:11:03.096 --> 00:11:04.526
I'm sorry.

00:11:04.691 --> 00:11:06.798
I don't mean to complain. No.

00:11:06.872 --> 00:11:10.262
Have you seen the rats or
have you just heard scratching?

00:11:11.344 --> 00:11:14.386
Just the scratching, actually. Mom?

00:11:18.784 --> 00:11:21.790
Ask them if it was here
when they lived here.

00:11:23.183 --> 00:11:24.228
What, Sari?

00:11:25.016 --> 00:11:26.739
The thing in my closet.

00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:31.056
Oh, no, baby, there was
nothing in their closets.

00:11:31.209 --> 00:11:32.011
Right?

00:11:32.836 --> 00:11:35.083
Right, no.No, of course not.

00:11:36.345 --> 00:11:38.958
She had a nightmare the other night.

00:11:39.073 --> 00:11:40.586
I wasn't dreaming.

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:44.186
It came into my bedroom,
and it was on fire.

00:11:45.179 --> 00:11:48.114
You heard that ? A figure on fire.

00:11:48.437 --> 00:11:50.785
And that woman Jenny, that was
the woman in your dreams? Yeah.

00:11:50.857 --> 00:11:53.607
And you hear what she was talking
about ? Scratching, flickering lights ?

00:11:53.683 --> 00:11:55.907
Both signs of a malevolent
spirit. Yeah well.

00:11:56.022 --> 00:11:58.161
I'm just freaked out your
weirdo visions are coming true.

00:11:58.177 --> 00:11:59.347
Forget about that for a minute.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.213
The thing in the house, do you think it's the
thing that killed mom and Jessica? I don't know!

00:12:02.439 --> 00:12:04.474
Has it come back or has it
been there the whole time?

00:12:04.479 --> 00:12:06.824
Maybe it's something else
entirely. Sam, we don't know yet.

00:12:06.833 --> 00:12:08.607
Those people are in danger, Dean.

00:12:09.023 --> 00:12:10.992
We have to get them out
of that house. And we will.

00:12:11.022 --> 00:12:12.832
No, I mean now. And how
you're gonna do that ?

00:12:12.849 --> 00:12:15.477
You got a story she's gonna believe?
Then what are we supposed to do?!

00:12:16.013 --> 00:12:17.741
We just got to chill out, that's all.

00:12:18.596 --> 00:12:20.953
If this was any other kind
of job, what would we do?

00:12:26.052 --> 00:12:27.949
We'd try to figure out
what we were dealing with.

00:12:28.503 --> 00:12:31.042
We'd dig into the history
of the house. Exactly.

00:12:31.065 --> 00:12:32.601
Except this time we
already know what happened.

00:12:32.634 --> 00:12:36.230
Yeah, but how much do we know?
How much do you actually remember?

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:40.118
About that night, you mean? Yeah.

00:12:42.063 --> 00:12:43.032
Not much.

00:12:44.484 --> 00:12:45.849
I remember the fire...

00:12:46.847 --> 00:12:47.742
The heat.

00:12:51.662 --> 00:12:53.158
Then I carried you out the front door.

00:12:55.902 --> 00:12:56.739
You did?

00:12:58.559 --> 00:12:59.982
Yeah, well, you never knew that?

00:13:02.309 --> 00:13:03.150
No.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.088
And, uh...

00:13:06.161 --> 00:13:08.641
Well, you know dad's story
as well as I do. Mom was...

00:13:10.182 --> 00:13:11.253
Was on the ceiling.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.555
Whatever put her there was long
gone by the time dad found her.

00:13:15.583 --> 00:13:18.277
And he never had a
theory about what did it?

00:13:18.782 --> 00:13:20.353
If he did, he kept it to himself.

00:13:21.264 --> 00:13:23.538
God knows we asked him enough times.

00:13:26.488 --> 00:13:27.324
Okay.

00:13:28.235 --> 00:13:30.744
So, if we're gonna figure
out what's going on now,

00:13:32.109 --> 00:13:33.914
We have to figure out
what happened back then,

00:13:35.191 --> 00:13:36.790
And see if it's the same thing.

00:13:36.952 --> 00:13:37.421
Yeah.

00:13:38.815 --> 00:13:41.904
Talk to dad's friends, neighbors,
people who were there at the time.

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:46.125
Does this feel like
just another job to you?

00:13:52.824 --> 00:13:54.599
I'll be right back. I
got to go to the bathroom.

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:14.922
<i>This is John Winchester.</i>

00:14:14.994 --> 00:14:21.289
<i>If this is an emergency, call
my son Dean, 866 907 32 35.</i>

00:14:21.333 --> 00:14:21.847
Dad...

00:14:25.062 --> 00:14:27.515
I know I've left you messages before.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.442
I don't even know if you get 'em.

00:14:33.441 --> 00:14:33.999
But

00:14:34.469 --> 00:14:35.584
I'm with Sam

00:14:36.626 --> 00:14:38.167
And we're in Lawrence,

00:14:39.179 --> 00:14:41.607
And there's something in our old house.

00:14:42.936 --> 00:14:45.688
I don't know if it's the
thing that killed mom or not,

00:14:47.151 --> 00:14:47.576
But...

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.982
I don't know what to do.

00:14:53.901 --> 00:14:54.679
So,

00:14:55.031 --> 00:14:57.293
Whatever you're doing,
if you could get here...

00:14:59.257 --> 00:15:00.123
Please.

00:15:02.751 --> 00:15:04.204
I need your help, dad.

00:15:09.282 --> 00:15:12.862
No, sir, nothing weird
down there. I promise.

00:15:13.361 --> 00:15:16.311
Sink just backed upon
its own. I'll take a look.

00:15:16.502 --> 00:15:17.426
Thanks.

00:15:18.556 --> 00:15:20.699
Oh, okay, I'll get out of your way.

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.743
So you and John Winchester, you
used to own this garage together?

00:17:06.816 --> 00:17:09.502
Yeah, we used to. A long time ago.

00:17:09.615 --> 00:17:10.495
Matter of fact,

00:17:10.715 --> 00:17:13.665
Must be 20 years since John disappeared.

00:17:13.809 --> 00:17:15.593
So, why are the cops
interested all of a sudden?

00:17:15.668 --> 00:17:19.660
Oh, we're reopening some of our unsolved cases,
and the Winchester disappearance is one of them.

00:17:19.754 --> 00:17:22.358
Uh-Huh. Well, what do you
want to know about John?

00:17:22.452 --> 00:17:24.692
Whatever you remember, you know.
Whatever sticks out in your mind.

00:17:28.228 --> 00:17:30.888
He was a stubborn
bastard. I remember that.

00:17:31.862 --> 00:17:33.059
And, uh...

00:17:33.117 --> 00:17:36.015
Oh, whatever the game, he
hated to lose, you know?

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.786
It was that whole marine thing.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:39.792
But, uh...

00:17:40.093 --> 00:17:41.536
Well, he sure loved Mary,

00:17:42.545 --> 00:17:44.034
And he doted on those kids.

00:17:44.515 --> 00:17:45.993
But that was before the fire.

00:17:47.081 --> 00:17:47.727
That's right.

00:17:48.043 --> 00:17:49.427
He ever talk about that night?

00:17:51.011 --> 00:17:51.606
No,

00:17:51.981 --> 00:17:53.025
Not at first.

00:17:53.717 --> 00:17:55.571
I think he was in shock. Right,

00:17:56.134 --> 00:17:57.529
But eventually,

00:17:58.597 --> 00:17:59.977
What did he say about it?

00:18:00.667 --> 00:18:03.504
Oh, he wasn't thinking
straight. He said, uh...

00:18:04.128 --> 00:18:07.613
He said something caused
that fire and killed Mary.

00:18:07.648 --> 00:18:08.678
He ever say what did it?

00:18:09.617 --> 00:18:12.136
Nothing did it. It was an accident.

00:18:12.537 --> 00:18:16.208
An electrical short in the
ceiling or walls or something.

00:18:18.156 --> 00:18:21.959
I begged him to get some
help, but... But what?

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.385
Oh, it just got worse and worse.

00:18:24.596 --> 00:18:25.135
How?

00:18:25.863 --> 00:18:29.382
Oh, he started reading
these strange old books.

00:18:29.417 --> 00:18:32.132
He started going to see
this palm reader in town.

00:18:32.305 --> 00:18:34.427
Palm reader? You have a name?

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:36.479
No.

00:18:40.598 --> 00:18:44.030
All right, so, there are a few
psychics and palm readers in town.

00:18:44.065 --> 00:18:46.510
There's someone named
El Divino. There's...

00:18:46.675 --> 00:18:49.443
There's the mysterious Mr. Fortinsky.

00:18:49.559 --> 00:18:52.198
Uh, Missouri Moseley,
some dude -- Wait, wait...

00:18:52.281 --> 00:18:53.407
Missouri Moseley?

00:18:53.735 --> 00:18:54.193
What?

00:18:54.509 --> 00:18:55.424
That's a psychic?

00:18:56.034 --> 00:18:58.732
Uh...yeah.Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:02.359 --> 00:19:03.263
In dad's journal...

00:19:06.653 --> 00:19:07.927
Look at this.

00:19:09.555 --> 00:19:11.957
First page, first sentence. Read that.

00:19:12.902 --> 00:19:14.228
"I went to Missouri...

00:19:15.483 --> 00:19:17.060
And I learned the truth."

00:19:17.887 --> 00:19:19.699
I always thought he meant the state.

00:19:25.511 --> 00:19:26.989
All right, then.

00:19:27.388 --> 00:19:29.347
Don't you worry about a thing.

00:19:30.156 --> 00:19:31.904
Your wife is crazy about you.

00:19:35.321 --> 00:19:37.959
Whew! Poor bastard.

00:19:38.463 --> 00:19:40.774
His woman cold-Bangin'the gardener.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:43.809
Why didn't you tell him?

00:19:44.203 --> 00:19:46.369
People don't come here for the truth.

00:19:46.404 --> 00:19:48.232
They come for good news.

00:19:49.739 --> 00:19:50.537
Well?

00:19:50.701 --> 00:19:53.960
Sam and Dean, come on
already. I ain't got all day.

00:20:02.075 --> 00:20:03.753
Well, let me look at you.

00:20:05.477 --> 00:20:08.493
Oh, you boys grew up handsome.

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.973
And you were one
goofy-Looking kid, too.

00:20:13.732 --> 00:20:14.765
Sam.

00:20:17.685 --> 00:20:19.163
Oh, honey.

00:20:21.052 --> 00:20:24.219
I'm sorry about your girlfriend.

00:20:24.829 --> 00:20:26.465
And your father

00:20:28.157 --> 00:20:29.681
he's missing?

00:20:32.614 --> 00:20:34.248
How'd you know all that?

00:20:34.283 --> 00:20:34.890
Well,

00:20:35.957 --> 00:20:38.840
You were just thinking it, just now.

00:20:39.361 --> 00:20:41.279
Well, where is he? Is he okay?

00:20:41.907 --> 00:20:43.318
I don't know.

00:20:43.983 --> 00:20:44.992
Don't know?

00:20:46.059 --> 00:20:47.775
You're supposed to be a psychic, right?

00:20:48.441 --> 00:20:52.542
Boy, you see me sawing
some bony tramp in half?

00:20:52.577 --> 00:20:53.974
You think I'm a magician?

00:20:54.212 --> 00:20:57.325
I may be able to read thoughts
and sense energies in a room,

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.548
But I can't just pull
facts out of thin air.

00:20:59.583 --> 00:21:00.021
Sit!

00:21:00.274 --> 00:21:00.904
Please.

00:21:10.994 --> 00:21:14.630
Boy, you put your foot on my coffee
table, I'm gonna whack you with a spoon.

00:21:14.665 --> 00:21:15.568
I didn't do anything.

00:21:15.653 --> 00:21:17.146
Well, you were thinking about it.

00:21:23.749 --> 00:21:25.384
Okay, so...

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:27.140
Our dad.

00:21:28.004 --> 00:21:29.461
When did you first meet him?

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.549
He came for a reading

00:21:32.245 --> 00:21:34.996
A few days after the fire.

00:21:35.884 --> 00:21:39.242
I just told him what was
really out there in the dark.

00:21:39.387 --> 00:21:41.108
I guess you could say

00:21:42.374 --> 00:21:44.467
I drew back the curtains for him.

00:21:44.493 --> 00:21:45.573
What about the fire?

00:21:46.991 --> 00:21:49.633
Do you know about what killed our mom?

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:50.734
A little.

00:21:51.674 --> 00:21:53.819
Your daddy took me to your house.

00:21:53.993 --> 00:21:55.771
He was hoping I could

00:21:55.916 --> 00:21:56.977
Sense the

00:21:57.446 --> 00:21:58.451
Echoes,

00:21:58.489 --> 00:22:00.507
The fingerprints of this thing.

00:22:00.865 --> 00:22:01.812
And could you?

00:22:02.393 --> 00:22:03.163
I don't...

00:22:04.954 --> 00:22:05.893
What was it?

00:22:06.578 --> 00:22:07.555
I don't know.

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.251
But it was evil.

00:22:12.463 --> 00:22:16.858
Look, I feel just awful
about the poor man's hand,

00:22:17.851 --> 00:22:20.521
But how can I be held liable?

00:22:22.884 --> 00:22:23.467
Yeah, but

00:22:23.626 --> 00:22:25.730
I can't afford a lawyer.

00:22:28.181 --> 00:22:30.892
Okay, listen, y-You just
got to let me call you back.

00:22:32.067 --> 00:22:35.108
Richie, mommy's gonna be right back,

00:22:35.333 --> 00:22:36.075
Okay?

00:22:36.169 --> 00:22:37.014
Okay.

00:22:37.437 --> 00:22:38.064
Okay.

00:22:42.177 --> 00:22:43.135
So,

00:22:44.683 --> 00:22:47.383
You think something's
back in that house?

00:22:48.348 --> 00:22:49.877
Definitely.

00:22:53.013 --> 00:22:54.813
I don't understand.

00:22:55.386 --> 00:22:56.540
What?

00:22:59.199 --> 00:23:01.011
I haven't been back inside,

00:23:01.046 --> 00:23:05.443
But I've been keeping an eye on
the place, and it's been quiet.

00:23:05.687 --> 00:23:07.786
No sudden deaths, no

00:23:07.947 --> 00:23:09.665
Freak accidents.

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:11.288
Why is it acting up now?

00:23:11.779 --> 00:23:12.633
I don't know.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:16.726
But dad going missing
and Jessica dying and

00:23:17.123 --> 00:23:18.677
Now this house,

00:23:19.188 --> 00:23:22.597
All happening at once. It just
feels like something's starting.

00:23:23.267 --> 00:23:25.392
That's a comforting thought.

00:23:56.438 --> 00:23:57.763
Juicy!

00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:16.031
Oh, baby, either we have
rats or mommy is going crazy.

00:24:16.745 --> 00:24:17.495
Richie?

00:24:20.229 --> 00:24:21.366
Richie?!

00:24:31.659 --> 00:24:33.997
Baby, where are you?!

00:24:42.328 --> 00:24:43.008
Wha...

00:24:51.117 --> 00:24:53.299
Mum! Oh, my god!

00:24:59.488 --> 00:25:00.661
Oh, baby!

00:25:03.724 --> 00:25:05.461
Sam, Dean,

00:25:05.836 --> 00:25:07.009
What are you doing here?

00:25:07.185 --> 00:25:08.276
Hey, Jenny.

00:25:08.546 --> 00:25:10.909
Um, this is our friend Missouri.

00:25:11.731 --> 00:25:15.068
If it's not too much trouble, we were
hoping to show her the house, you know,

00:25:15.231 --> 00:25:17.139
For old time's sake.

00:25:17.174 --> 00:25:19.428
No, you know, this isn't a good time.

00:25:19.463 --> 00:25:21.424
I'm kind of busy. Listen,
Jenny,it's important.

00:25:21.569 --> 00:25:22.058
Ow!

00:25:22.419 --> 00:25:25.738
Give the poor girl a break.
Can't you see she's upset?

00:25:25.773 --> 00:25:27.204
Forgive this boy. He means well.

00:25:27.239 --> 00:25:29.275
He's just not the
sharpest tool in the shed.

00:25:29.310 --> 00:25:30.691
But hear me out.

00:25:31.295 --> 00:25:32.401
About what?

00:25:32.459 --> 00:25:33.725
About this house.

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:35.902
What are you talking about?

00:25:36.397 --> 00:25:39.125
I think you know what I'm talking about.

00:25:39.160 --> 00:25:44.091
You think there's something in this house,
something that wants to hurt your family.

00:25:44.126 --> 00:25:45.580
Am I mistaken?

00:25:46.514 --> 00:25:48.251
Who are you?

00:25:48.286 --> 00:25:51.554
We're people who can help,
who can stop this thing,

00:25:51.589 --> 00:25:54.042
But you're gonna have to
trust us, just a little.

00:25:56.764 --> 00:26:01.968
If there's a dark energy around here,
this room should be the center of it.

00:26:03.317 --> 00:26:04.128
Why?

00:26:04.658 --> 00:26:07.335
This used to be your nursery, Sam.

00:26:07.370 --> 00:26:09.646
This is where it all happened.

00:26:24.935 --> 00:26:26.612
That an emf?

00:26:27.006 --> 00:26:27.592
Yeah.

00:26:28.552 --> 00:26:29.399
Amateur.

00:26:39.764 --> 00:26:42.602
I don't know if you boys should
be disappointed or relieved,

00:26:42.637 --> 00:26:44.818
But this ain't the
thing that took your mom.

00:26:46.478 --> 00:26:47.906
Are you sure?

00:26:48.887 --> 00:26:50.113
How do you know?

00:26:50.119 --> 00:26:53.921
It isn't the same energy I
felt the last time I was here.

00:26:53.956 --> 00:26:55.368
It's something different.

00:26:56.353 --> 00:26:57.375
What is it?

00:26:59.004 --> 00:27:00.495
Not it...

00:27:01.253 --> 00:27:02.797
Them.

00:27:03.411 --> 00:27:06.478
There's more than one
spirit in this place.

00:27:07.634 --> 00:27:09.246
What are they doing here?

00:27:09.281 --> 00:27:12.140
They're here because of
what happened to your family.

00:27:12.734 --> 00:27:14.636
You see, all those years ago,

00:27:14.728 --> 00:27:17.268
Real evil came to you.

00:27:18.648 --> 00:27:23.242
It walked this house. That
kind of evil leaves wounds,

00:27:23.277 --> 00:27:26.050
And sometimes wounds get infected.

00:27:26.366 --> 00:27:28.098
I don't understand.

00:27:28.133 --> 00:27:31.408
This place is a magnet
for paranormal energy.

00:27:34.222 --> 00:27:36.632
It's attracted a poltergeist,

00:27:37.087 --> 00:27:38.760
A nasty one,

00:27:39.527 --> 00:27:43.288
And it won't rest until
Jenny and her babies are dead.

00:27:43.323 --> 00:27:45.552
You said there was more than one spirit.

00:27:45.641 --> 00:27:47.144
There is.

00:27:50.004 --> 00:27:53.301
I just can't quite
make out the second one.

00:27:57.361 --> 00:27:59.205
Well, one thing's for damn sure,

00:27:59.793 --> 00:28:01.630
Nobody's dying in this house,

00:28:01.665 --> 00:28:02.804
Ever again.

00:28:03.484 --> 00:28:05.835
So, whatever is here, how do we stop it?

00:28:09.249 --> 00:28:11.370
So, what is all this stuff anyway?

00:28:11.811 --> 00:28:15.250
Angelica root, van van
oil, crossroad dirt,

00:28:15.305 --> 00:28:17.241
A few other odds and ends.

00:28:17.276 --> 00:28:18.505
What are we supposed to do with it?

00:28:18.540 --> 00:28:21.712
We're gonna put them inside the walls

00:28:21.928 --> 00:28:25.160
In the north, south, east, west corners

00:28:25.195 --> 00:28:27.127
On each floor of the house.

00:28:27.162 --> 00:28:30.270
Punching holes in the drywall.
Jenny's gonna love that.

00:28:31.230 --> 00:28:32.647
She'll live.

00:28:33.715 --> 00:28:35.958
And this will destroy the spirits?

00:28:35.993 --> 00:28:37.270
It should.

00:28:37.840 --> 00:28:40.461
It should purify the house completely.

00:28:41.604 --> 00:28:43.270
We'll each take a floor,

00:28:43.633 --> 00:28:45.143
But we work fast.

00:28:45.178 --> 00:28:48.039
Once the spirits
realize what we're up to,

00:28:48.067 --> 00:28:50.198
Things are gonna get bad.

00:28:51.969 --> 00:28:52.821
Okay.

00:28:54.151 --> 00:28:55.534
Careful.

00:28:57.037 --> 00:29:00.847
Look, I -You know, I'm not sure I'm
comfortable leaving you guys here alone.

00:29:00.882 --> 00:29:03.181
Just take your kids to
the movie or something, and

00:29:03.219 --> 00:29:05.373
It'll be over by the time you get back.

00:29:06.245 --> 00:29:06.937
Okay.

00:30:03.621 --> 00:30:05.372
Aah! Uhh!

00:30:43.430 --> 00:30:44.205
Sam!

00:30:46.516 --> 00:30:47.255
Sam!

00:31:10.277 --> 00:31:11.469
Come on.

00:31:33.245 --> 00:31:35.130
Are you sure this is over?

00:31:38.299 --> 00:31:39.609
I'm sure.

00:31:40.037 --> 00:31:40.646
Why?

00:31:41.796 --> 00:31:43.483
Why do you ask?

00:31:44.338 --> 00:31:45.929
No, never mind.

00:31:47.634 --> 00:31:49.481
It's nothing, I guess.

00:31:51.517 --> 00:31:52.840
Hello?

00:31:53.417 --> 00:31:54.896
We're home.

00:31:57.933 --> 00:31:59.541
What happened?

00:31:59.645 --> 00:32:02.316
Hi. Sorry. Um, we'll...

00:32:02.351 --> 00:32:04.381
We'll pay for all of this.

00:32:05.143 --> 00:32:06.575
Don't you worry.

00:32:06.633 --> 00:32:08.698
Dean's gonna clean up this mess.

00:32:11.724 --> 00:32:13.707
Well, what are you waiting for, boy?

00:32:13.742 --> 00:32:14.510
Get the mop.

00:32:15.414 --> 00:32:16.974
And don't cuss at me.

00:32:38.504 --> 00:32:39.267
Okay.

00:33:33.226 --> 00:33:35.331
So, tell me again. What
are we still doing here?

00:33:35.366 --> 00:33:36.827
I don't know, I-I just...

00:33:37.472 --> 00:33:39.056
I still have a bad feeling.

00:33:39.642 --> 00:33:40.651
Why?

00:33:41.167 --> 00:33:44.812
Missouri did her whole zelda rubenstein thing.
The house should be clean. This should be over.

00:33:45.037 --> 00:33:47.946
Yeah, probably, but I just
want to make sure. That's all.

00:33:49.410 --> 00:33:52.466
The problem is I could be
sleeping in a bed right now.

00:33:56.837 --> 00:33:57.775
Dean!

00:33:58.256 --> 00:33:58.956
Dean!

00:34:00.915 --> 00:34:02.759
You grab the kids, I'll get Jenny.

00:34:21.418 --> 00:34:23.119
Come on! Jenny!

00:34:23.157 --> 00:34:25.775
I can't open the door! Stand back!

00:34:28.841 --> 00:34:30.342
Come on! No, my kids!

00:34:30.349 --> 00:34:31.469
Sam's got your kids. Come on.

00:34:34.221 --> 00:34:35.315
Help!

00:34:35.972 --> 00:34:37.086
Please!

00:34:40.699 --> 00:34:41.813
Come here.

00:34:42.514 --> 00:34:44.106
Don't look, don't look.

00:34:57.454 --> 00:35:00.742
Sari, take your brother outside as
fast as you can and don't look back.

00:35:09.028 --> 00:35:10.617
Are you okay, baby?

00:35:10.640 --> 00:35:13.500
Sari, where's Sam? He's
inside. Something's got him.

00:35:35.772 --> 00:35:37.694
Ugh! Aah!

00:36:00.741 --> 00:36:01.319
Sam!

00:36:22.050 --> 00:36:22.881
Sam?!

00:36:23.782 --> 00:36:24.307
Sam!

00:36:29.062 --> 00:36:31.200
No, don't! Don't! What? Why?

00:36:32.513 --> 00:36:33.993
Because I know who it is.

00:36:34.769 --> 00:36:36.487
I can see her now.

00:36:53.613 --> 00:36:54.949
Mom.

00:37:05.264 --> 00:37:06.569
Dean.

00:37:21.916 --> 00:37:23.366
Sam.

00:37:29.844 --> 00:37:31.501
I'm sorry.

00:37:36.221 --> 00:37:37.883
F-For what?

00:37:50.190 --> 00:37:53.055
You, get out of my house.

00:37:53.872 --> 00:37:56.191
And let go of my son.

00:38:26.398 --> 00:38:27.970
Now it's over.

00:38:41.689 --> 00:38:42.943
Thanks for these.

00:38:43.455 --> 00:38:45.558
Don't thank me. They're yours.

00:38:50.269 --> 00:38:51.143
Well,

00:38:51.622 --> 00:38:55.218
There are no spirits in there
anymore, this time for sure.

00:38:56.402 --> 00:38:58.075
Not even my mom?

00:38:58.740 --> 00:39:00.075
No.

00:39:04.432 --> 00:39:05.921
What happened?

00:39:06.968 --> 00:39:11.625
Your mom's spirit and the poltergeists'
energy, they canceled each other out.

00:39:12.115 --> 00:39:15.704
Your mom destroyed herself
going after the thing.

00:39:16.961 --> 00:39:19.222
Why would she do something like that?

00:39:20.270 --> 00:39:23.349
Well, to protect her boys, of course.

00:39:31.224 --> 00:39:33.220
Sam, I'm sorry.

00:39:35.573 --> 00:39:36.963
For what?

00:39:37.493 --> 00:39:40.355
You sensed it was here, didn't you?

00:39:40.390 --> 00:39:42.115
Even when I couldn't.

00:39:47.123 --> 00:39:48.874
What's happening to me?

00:39:49.837 --> 00:39:52.839
I know I should have
all the answers, but...

00:39:54.540 --> 00:39:55.967
I don't know.

00:39:56.541 --> 00:39:57.984
Sam, you ready ?

00:40:03.044 --> 00:40:04.174
Bye.

00:40:07.167 --> 00:40:08.542
Bye Sam.

00:40:11.053 --> 00:40:12.213
Ah.

00:40:12.894 --> 00:40:15.235
Don't you boys be strangers.

00:40:15.658 --> 00:40:16.891
We won't.

00:40:18.438 --> 00:40:19.692
See you around.

00:40:50.999 --> 00:40:52.596
That boy...

00:40:54.228 --> 00:40:56.108
He has such

00:40:56.200 --> 00:40:58.195
Powerful abilities.

00:41:01.970 --> 00:41:04.707
Why he couldn't sense his own father,

00:41:04.919 --> 00:41:06.537
I have no idea.

00:41:12.289 --> 00:41:13.426
Mary's spirit...

00:41:15.219 --> 00:41:17.521
Do you really think she saved the boys?

00:41:19.860 --> 00:41:20.809
I do.

00:41:32.792 --> 00:41:35.515
John Winchester, I could just slap you.

00:41:35.581 --> 00:41:38.035
Why don't you go talk to your children?

00:41:39.667 --> 00:41:41.179
God, I want to.

00:41:43.164 --> 00:41:45.662
You have no idea how
much I want to see them.

00:41:48.602 --> 00:41:49.556
But I can't.

00:41:51.218 --> 00:41:51.923
Not yet.

00:41:58.463 --> 00:42:00.238
Not until I know the truth.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
